2026-11-13T10:02:14.1729713Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-13T10:02:14.1739444Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-13T10:02:14.1740088Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-13T10:02:14.1740443Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-13T10:02:14.1740614Z 
2026-11-13T10:02:14.1740761Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-13T10:02:14.1741053Z 
2026-11-13T10:02:14.1741293Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-13T10:02:14.1741665Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-13T10:02:14.1742069Z 
2026-11-13T10:02:14.1742187Z If you would like to
2026-11-13T10:02:14.1742481Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-13T10:02:14.1742725Z 
2026-11-13T10:02:14.1742983Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-13T10:02:14.1743512Z   $ sh ./install-nix
